    "result_text": "All done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created.\n\n**New helper \u2014 `Addresses.java`** (in `rest/function/owner/`): a `normalize(String)` method matching the existing `Telephones`/`OwnerEmails` pattern. It trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-token abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`), returning `\"\"` for null/blank input.\n\n**`BuildOwner`**: normalizes the address into the request *before* the required-field loop, so:\n- the stored/returned `address` is the normalized form (mapped onto the `Owner` entity), and\n- the required-field check now rejects an address that is blank *after* normalization (e.g. `\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400).\n\n**`EnsureUniqueHousehold`** and **`AssignHousehold`**: both address comparisons (duplicate detection and the shared household-id derivation) now use `Addresses.normalize(...)` for both the new owner and each existing owner, so comparisons \u2014 and the derived `householdId` \u2014 use the normalized form. Their local `normalize` remains for the last-name comparison; javadoc updated to match.\n\nTest results:\n- 3 new acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesWhitespaceAndCase`, `functionalityExpandsAbbreviations`, `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`) pass.\n- Full `mvnw -o test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 3 run / 0 failures / 0 errors.",
